Before diving into the best practices, please note that you may need to adapt the globs depending on your specific project structure.

---
name: vue3-best-practices.mdc
description: Best practices for Vue 3 applications using Composition API
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}
---

- Use the Composition API for better code organization and reusability
- Implement proper reactivity with `ref` and `reactive`
- Use `provide/inject` for dependency injection
- Leverage `script setup` syntax for concise component definitions

---
name: tailwindcss-best-practices.mdc
description: Best practices for styling with Tailwind CSS
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx,css}
---

- Use utility-first classes for rapid development
- Create custom components with `@apply` directive
- Implement responsive design using breakpoints
- Optimize build size with `@tailwindcss/jit`

---
name: primevue4-best-practices.mdc
description: Best practices for using PrimeVue 4 components
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}
---

- Use PrimeVue components for consistent UI across the application
- Customize themes using PrimeVue's theming system
- Implement proper accessibility features provided by PrimeVue
- Optimize performance by lazy-loading components when possible

---
name: typescript-best-practices.mdc
description: TypeScript coding standards and type safety guidelines
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx}
---

- Use strict null checks to prevent null/undefined errors
- Prefer interfaces over types for better extensibility
- Implement type guards and assertions for runtime type checking
- Use enums for a set of named constants